# Git normalises line endings on checkout, and on Windows that means CRLF. For anything
# executed on Linux a carriage return is not the end of the line, it is the last character
# of the command: `set -euo pipefail\r` fails with "invalid option name", and a Dockerfile's
# trailing backslash stops continuing the line it is on.
#
# These are the files that cross to a Linux host and are run there.
bin/deploy          text eol=lf
gradlew             text eol=lf
*.sh                text eol=lf
Dockerfile          text eol=lf
compose.yaml        text eol=lf
